STEP 0 — THE HEAP IN C++ (READ THIS FIRST)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

// Max-heap (default) — top() gives the LARGEST element
priority_queue<int> maxH;

// Min-heap — top() gives the SMALLEST element
priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> minH;

// Min-heap of pairs {value, index}
priority_queue<pair<int,int>, vector<pair<int,int>>, greater<>> minH;

// Common operations — all O(log n) except top() which is O(1)
minH.push(x);       // insert
minH.pop();         // remove top
minH.top();         // peek (does NOT remove)
minH.size();
minH.empty();
KEY RULE:
Max-heap → top() = largest → use to MAINTAIN THE MINIMUM (kick out the max)
Min-heap → top() = smallest → use to MAINTAIN THE MAXIMUM (kick out the min)

This sounds backwards. It becomes natural once you see the patterns.

