TYPE 3 — TWO HEAPS (Median / Balance Problems)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

When to use:
→ Find or maintain the median of a stream
→ Problems that need to track both the "upper half" and "lower half"
→ Any problem needing the middle element dynamically

Keywords: "median", "balance", "stream of numbers"

KEY INSIGHT:
Split numbers into two halves:
Left half → Max-heap (top = largest of the smaller half)
Right half → Min-heap (top = smallest of the larger half)

Median:
Even count → average of maxH.top() and minH.top()
Odd count → top of the larger heap

After every insert, rebalance so |maxH.size() - minH.size()| <= 1.

TEMPLATE — Add Number + Get Median:

priority_queue<int> maxH;                            // left half
priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> minH; // right half

void addNum(int num) {
    // Always push to maxH first
    maxH.push(num);

    // Ensure all of maxH <= all of minH
    if (!minH.empty() && maxH.top() > minH.top()) {
        minH.push(maxH.top()); maxH.pop();
    }

    // Balance sizes: maxH can have at most 1 extra
    if (maxH.size() > minH.size() + 1) {
        minH.push(maxH.top()); maxH.pop();
    } else if (minH.size() > maxH.size()) {
        maxH.push(minH.top()); minH.pop();
    }
}

double findMedian() {
    if (maxH.size() > minH.size()) return maxH.top();
    return (maxH.top() + minH.top()) / 2.0;
}
