TYPE 5 — LAZY DELETION (Heap + Hashmap)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

When to use:
→ Elements need to be "removed" from the heap but heap doesn't support deletion
→ Sliding window with a heap
→ Elements get invalidated over time

KEY INSIGHT:
You cannot efficiently remove an arbitrary element from a heap.
Instead, mark it as "deleted" in a hashmap.
When you pop from the heap, skip any element that was marked deleted.

TEMPLATE — Lazy Deletion:

priority_queue<int> maxH;  // or min-heap
unordered_map<int, int> deleted;  // value → how many times it's been deleted

void remove(int val) {
    deleted[val]++;
}

int top() {
    // Skip deleted entries
    while (!maxH.empty() && deleted[maxH.top()] > 0) {
        deleted[maxH.top()]--;
        maxH.pop();
    }
    return maxH.top();
}
